english:
Where tiny millet-grains with blossoms mingle, and a lamb is slain;
where the banner of the rooster, with its war-cry, stands proudly raised;
in the glorious festivals held from village to village,
where devotees praise, and He manifests in forms beyond reach;
in the frenzied dance-grounds where the Vēlaṉ performs his rites;
in forests and groves, in beautiful river-islands,
by rivers and ponds, and diverse settlements;
at crossroads and meeting-places, beneath fresh-blossomed Kaṭampu trees;
in public squares and shelters, and at sites with sacred pillars.
